    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="12" relname="concession">While I agree with the additional factors that you include in understanding learnability,</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="12" relname="span">I like the Ten-Minute Rule described in our text.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="14" relname="unless">Unless the application is complex,</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="14" relname="span">the user should be able to learn how to use the system in under 10 minutes.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="15" relname="span">Frankly, I find that I have behaved much that way in my own experience.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="17" relname="unless">Unless I want to sit down and become an expert</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="17" relname="span">I prefer to see progress and some results; fast.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="18" relname="span">A current example for me is completing my income tax.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="10" relname="concession">While occasionally I have needed professional assistance,</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="19" relname="span">I tried a couple of packages until I found one that is easy to "learn".</segment>
        <group id="11" type="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="11" relname="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="2" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="13" relname="span"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="4" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="5" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="16" relname="span"/>
        <group id="18" type="span" parent="7" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="8" relname="elaboration"/>
    </body>
</rst>
